course: dictionary
lesson: 11068
title: Words about floating
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weightless means having no weight, or seeming to have no weight. You can spot its clue inside the word: weight plus less, meaning without weight. «The astronauts floated weightless inside the space station.» Floating with no weight tells you the meaning fits.
explain: Astronauts still have mass, so they are not empty. They feel weightless because they and the station are falling around the Earth together. Falling freely makes them seem to have no weight, even though gravity still pulls on them.
explain: The word is not only about space. «At the top of a swing you feel almost weightless.» Almost weightless means very light, like a feather. The clue is the word almost, which tells you the feeling is close to having no weight, but not quite.
fact: Weightless means having no weight, or seeming to have no weight.
fact: «Weightless» is made from weight and -less, which means without.
fact: Astronauts still have mass when they float; they feel weightless because they fall around the Earth together with their station.
fact: «Almost weightless» means very light, like a feather.
fact: Gravity at the International Space Station is about 90% as strong as on the ground.
exercise: «The astronauts floated weightless inside the station.» What does weightless mean? | Very heavy and slow | Wet and cold | *Having no weight, or seeming to have none | Dressed in thick, warm clothes
exercise: «At the top of the swing you feel almost weightless.» What does almost weightless suggest? | Very heavy, like a stone | Fast asleep in bed | Hungry and tired | *Very light, like a feather
exercise: Why do astronauts feel weightless in space? | Because they are standing on a swing | *Because they and the station fall together around the Earth | Because they are very small | Because there is no air at all in the room
test: Which two smaller words make up weightless? | *weight and less | wet and light | way and less | wait and less
test: Astronauts still have mass in space. What does weightless mean for them? | They weigh more than on Earth | They have no mass at all | They are stuck firmly to the floor | *They seem to have no weight, because they fall with the station
exam: What is the opposite of weightless in «At the bottom of a swing you feel heaviest»? | Hollow | Empty | *Heavy | Floating
